@startuml fig04_class_scheduler
!include theme.iuml
title Figure 4 — Class View: Scheduler Core and the Five-Policy Factorial

skinparam linetype ortho

interface DispatchPolicy <<interface>> {
  +name : str
  +choose(request : Request, node_states : list[NodeState], now : float, rng : Random) : NodeId
}

class RoundRobin <<queue-blind · hw-blind>> {
  -cursor : int
}
class JSQ <<queue-aware · hw-blind>> {
  +choose() : NodeId
}
class StaticWeighted <<queue-blind · hw-aware>> {
  -weights : dict[NodeId, float]
}
class WJSQ <<queue-aware · hw-aware>> {
  +score(n : NodeState) : float
}
class ThresholdT <<degenerate baseline, H2>> {
  -T : float
}

DispatchPolicy <|.. RoundRobin
DispatchPolicy <|.. JSQ
DispatchPolicy <|.. StaticWeighted
DispatchPolicy <|.. WJSQ
DispatchPolicy <|.. ThresholdT

' --- arrange the four factorial cells as a 2x2 block ---
RoundRobin -[hidden]right- JSQ
StaticWeighted -[hidden]right- WJSQ
RoundRobin -[hidden]down- StaticWeighted
JSQ -[hidden]down- WJSQ
WJSQ -[hidden]right- ThresholdT

note bottom of WJSQ
  The four cells above form the **2x2 factorial** of §4.1: hardware-awareness
  crossed with queue-awareness. H1 is a statement about the interaction term,
  which a policy *ladder* could not decompose.
end note

class PolicyFactory {
  +{static} from_config(name : str, params : dict) : DispatchPolicy
}
PolicyFactory ..> DispatchPolicy : creates

class Scheduler {
  -policy : DispatchPolicy
  -view : CapabilityView
  -admission : AdmissionFilter
  -logger : DecisionLogger
  +on_request(r : Request, now : float) : Dispatch
}
Scheduler o--> DispatchPolicy
Scheduler o--> CapabilityView
Scheduler o--> AdmissionFilter
Scheduler ..> DecisionRecord : emits

class Request {
  +req_id : str
  +scheduled_offset : float
  +prompt_tokens : int
  +output_tokens : int
  +length_bucket : str
  +priority : Tier
  +content_seed : int
}

class NodeState {
  +node_id : NodeId
  +queue_depth : int
  +in_flight : list[InFlightItem]
  +recent_tok_s : float
  +kv_occupancy : float
  +observed_at : float
  +estimate_age(now : float) : float
}

class InFlightItem {
  +length_bucket : str
  +tokens_remaining_est : int
}
NodeState *--> "0..*" InFlightItem

class CapabilityView {
  -staleness_s : float
  -latest : dict[NodeId, NodeState]
  +on_heartbeat(hb : Heartbeat) : void
  +as_of(now : float) : list[NodeState]
}
CapabilityView ..> NodeState : serves aged copies
CapabilityView o--> CostModel

class StalenessInjector <<F-8>> {
  +s : float
  +age(view : CapabilityView, now : float) : list[NodeState]
}
CapabilityView *--> StalenessInjector

abstract class CostModel <<F-6 / F-7>> {
  +fitted_at : float
  +n_parameters : int
  +{abstract} expected_service_time(prompt_tokens : int, predicted_output_tokens : int, live : NodeState) : float
}
class BucketedLookupCostModel {
  -table : dict[bucket, float]
}
class LowParamRegression {
  -params : float[<= 6]
}
CostModel <|-- BucketedLookupCostModel
CostModel <|-- LowParamRegression

class AdmissionFilter <<F-13 / F-14>> {
  +timeout_ceiling : float
  +admissible(r : Request, n : NodeState) : bool
  +candidates(r : Request, ns : list[NodeState]) : list[NodeState]
}

class DecisionRecord <<F-3>> {
  +req_id : str
  +policy : str
  +chosen : NodeId
  +candidates : list[NodeId]
  +queue_depths : dict[NodeId, int]
  +capability_estimates : dict[NodeId, float]
  +estimate_ages : dict[NodeId, float]
  +scores : dict[NodeId, float]
  +decided_at : float
}

Scheduler ..> Request
DispatchPolicy ..> Request : reads
DispatchPolicy ..> NodeState : reads
WJSQ ..> CostModel : weights by expected service time

note top of DispatchPolicy
  Pure function. Clock and randomness are **injected**, never read from the
  ambient process — so one implementation runs unchanged in the live
  scheduler and in the discrete-event simulator (F-2, F-21).
end note

note right of ThresholdT
  Round-robin over nodes above cutoff T. Exists to test **H2**: as R grows,
  the hardware-aware policy should collapse onto this one-line rule.
end note

note bottom of AdmissionFilter
  Applied to **every** policy including the baselines, so no policy is charged
  with infinite-latency outcomes it merely failed to avoid (F-14).
end note
@enduml
